---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaBanner from '../components/CtaBanner.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Deep Service Breakdown & Engineering Scope | Soale Astra"
  description="Comprehensive technical specifications and deliverable breakdown for Soale Astra's product design, design systems, and AI interaction engineering."
>
  <section class="py-20 sm:py-28 bg-neutral-950 text-white relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 dark-grid-backdrop opacity-25 pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
        <a href="/services" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors mb-2">
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
            <path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path>
          </svg>
          <span>Back to Services Overview</span>
        </a>
        <h1 class="display-hero font-display font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white">
          Deep Service Scope &amp; Deliverables Matrix
        </h1>
        <p class="display-subhead text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          A granular view into our design specifications, token structures, prototyping fidelity, and engineering pairing guidelines.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 sm:py-28 bg-white text-neutral-900">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-16">
      
      <!-- Section 1: Design Systems Architecture -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-md bg-indigo-50 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-indigo-700">
          Module A // System Foundations
        </div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-neutral-950">
          Multi-Brand Design Tokens &amp; Component Hierarchies
        </h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-base leading-relaxed">
          We don't just supply static Figma components. Our studio delivers tokenized structures exportable to JSON, CSS Custom Properties, and Tailwind configurations:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 pt-2">
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200">
            <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-neutral-900 mb-2">Global Tokens</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">Semantic color primitives, fluid typographic scales (clamp-based), elevation shadows, and modular spacing units.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200">
            <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-neutral-900 mb-2">Alias Tokens</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">Contextual mapping for surfaces, brand accents, disabled states, and light/dark theme inversions.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200">
            <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-neutral-900 mb-2">Component Tokens</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">Scattered override tokens for buttons, inputs, data grids, modal dialogues, and streaming text containers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 2: AI UX & Latency Ergonomics -->
      <div class="space-y-6 pt-12 border-t border-neutral-200">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-md bg-cyan-50 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-cyan-800">
          Module B // Stochastic Interaction
        </div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-neutral-950">
          AI &amp; Agentic Interface Ergonomics
        </h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-base leading-relaxed">
          LLMs and generative models introduce latency and unpredictability. Our specialized AI interaction stack solves these specific failure modes:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-sm text-neutral-700">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200">
            <span class="text-indigo-600 font-bold">01</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="font-display text-neutral-900 block mb-0.5">Micro-Latency Masking</strong>
              <span>Skeleton streams, progressive token reveal curves, and non-blocking background workers that keep the interface responsive while models generate output.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200">
            <span class="text-indigo-600 font-bold">02</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="font-display text-neutral-900 block mb-0.5">Confidence Scoring &amp; Source Verification</strong>
              <span>Clear visual indicators for verified claims, inline citation popovers, and model reasoning accordions that instill user trust without cluttering the screen.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200">
            <span class="text-indigo-600 font-bold">03</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="font-display text-neutral-900 block mb-0.5">Multi-Agent Workflow Schemas</strong>
              <span>Split-canvas viewports, background task orchestrators, and human-in-the-loop review queues for complex enterprise decision systems.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 3: Engineering Pairing SLA -->
      <div class="space-y-6 pt-12 border-t border-neutral-200">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-md bg-emerald-50 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-emerald-800">
          Module C // Integration &amp; Handoff
        </div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-neutral-950">
          Direct Engineering Collaboration
        </h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-base leading-relaxed">
          Designers who cannot read code or review Pull Requests create bottlenecks. Soale Astra works directly alongside your engineering leads:
        </p>
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-neutral-950 text-white font-mono text-xs space-y-3">
          <div class="text-indigo-400">// Engineering Pairing Standard Protocol</div>
          <div class="text-neutral-400">1. Async Loom walk-through of every high-fidelity screen state</div>
          <div class="text-neutral-400">2. Pixel-level staging branch audit prior to customer deployment</div>
          <div class="text-neutral-400">3. WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility automated + manual keyboard navigation test</div>
          <div class="text-emerald-400">4. Zero broken states or ambiguous component behaviors guaranteed</div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBanner />
</Layout>
